Package: swbrd-ext-puddle
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Evan Brass <brassevan@gmail.com>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: swbrd-common (>= @COMPAT@), swbrd-dtls-proxy (>= @COMPAT@), systemd, init-system-helpers (>= 1.54), libc6 (>= 2.38), libgcc-s1
Homepage: https://github.com/evan-brass/swbrd
Description: Puddle, the back end of the Rainboots chat client
 Serves the rainboots.v1 datachannel protocol: a roster of who is connected, a
 single room per host, IRC-style nicks secured by a password, and a relay for
 the ICE candidates two peers need to build a direct connection to each other.
 .
 A candidate is only relayed when the sender's claimed peer id matches the
 certificate fingerprint the daemon authenticated, so the relay cannot be used
 to impersonate anybody.  Nothing said in the room is stored, and there is no
 scrollback to hand over.
 .
 Built for one private host and not fit for redistribution; see
 /usr/share/doc/swbrd-ext-puddle/copyright.
